// The subsurface material feature
//
// The first material feature — the second source of G-buffer channel
// requests, after lighting models (plan2 P12, ADR 0037). A feature owns a
// channel on the models' behalf: this module declares the channel's macro
// knob, and `pack_subsurface` produces the value the channel carries when
// a material's graph pins `wxsl_subsurface: true`.
//
// The strength is a macro *constant* for now, pinned per material like any
// graph macro — which makes it part of the variant cache key, so a
// material with a different strength is a different compiled shader, not a
// different uniform. A surface-driven strength (a graph node writing it
// into the `Surface`) needs a `Surface` field, which is a schema change
// recorded when the first such feature lands.
//
// No shipped lighting model reads the channel yet: a feature-aware model
// reads `extras.subsurface` in its dispatch arm, and that model is the
// first real subsurface model's work. The channel, its packing and its
// round trip through the G-buffer are what this feature provides.

// Turns the feature on for a material, and asks its pipeline for the
// channel. Declared here so a material pinning it is an ordinary macro
// pin; the renderer's feature check reads the same name.
@macro const wxsl_subsurface: bool = false;

// The strength the channel carries, in 0..1. A macro const rather than a
// uniform parameter: it shapes the generated pack, and the variant cache
// keys on it.
@macro const wxsl_subsurface_strength: f32 = 0.0;

// Produces the channel's value: `(strength, radius)` — radius is here so
// a model has a second quantity to consume without a second feature, and
// stays 0 until a model gives it a convention.
fn pack_subsurface() -> vec2f {
    return vec2f(wxsl_subsurface_strength, 0.0);
}
